          <h3>Other Notable Moons</h3>
          <p>Beyond the Galilean moons, Jupiter has dozens of smaller satellites. Amalthea, the largest inner moon, orbits within Jupiter's ring system and contributes material to the rings. The remaining moons are mostly small, irregular objects—likely captured asteroids and comets. Many of these outer moons orbit in retrograde (opposite to Jupiter's rotation), suggesting they were captured rather than forming alongside Jupiter.</p>
