    },
    thermosphere: {
      name: 'Thermosphere', alt: '320 – 1,000 km',
      desc: "An unexpectedly hot layer — temperatures reach 700–1,000 K, far higher than solar heating alone can explain. Jupiter's powerful auroras deposit enormous energy here, driving heating across the entire globe. This 'energy crisis' of gas giant thermospheres is an active area of planetary science research.",
      fact: "✦ Jupiter's aurora is hundreds of times more energetic than Earth's and permanently active at both poles.",
